@prefix : <http://example.org/orexis/world/terrace#> .
@prefix orexis: <http://example.org/orexis#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix speech: <http://example.org/orexis/speech#> .
@prefix telegram: <http://example.org/orexis/telegram#> .

<> a orexis:SocietyGraph .    # this document is one graph, and this is what it is

#  WHO SPEAKS WITH WHOM, THROUGH WHAT: the terrace's agent with its sovereign, in a Telegram chat
#  through the agent's own bot (society.ttl). The agent wants nothing and says nothing of its own;
#  what the chat carries is what it observes, queried when a question asks it.
#  The chat's id is the sovereign's and sits in secrets/terrace/chat.ttl, not here.

#  WHAT THE MODEL MAY READ IN IT: everything the agent holds, and what happened to it - its journal and its
#  series - since the chat is with its sovereign; and the sovereign may state anything in the world's words, a
#  sensor's defect among them, since theirs is the world's word (knowledge/domain/speech/chat.md).
:terrace_and_dmitrii a speech:Chat ;
    speech:participant :terrace_agent , :dmitrii ;
    speech:channel :sovereign_telegram ;
    speech:reads orexis:Graph , orexis:Event ;
    speech:allows rdf:Property .
:sovereign_telegram a telegram:Chat .
